{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":27294,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"041f6ae6849c0a7a9a5e63763d66c4ba","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see the media assets clearly. Now I understand the visual language. Let me check what the avatar Maria looks like - it's 108x72 wide (not square). Card texture is coral gradient. Logo VISA is white on gray. Logo Mastercard has red/orange circles.\n\nNow let me start building. My plan:\n\n**Workspace setup:**\n- 6 frames at 375×812 in a row (01_Get_Started, 02_Home, 03_Wallet, 04_Add_Card, 05_Payment, 06_Receipt)\n- Reusable components in workspace\n\n**Design system:**\n- Brand: #007AFF (iOS blue)\n- Neutrals: #1A1A1F (text), #8E8E93 (secondary text), #F2F2F7 (bg surface), #FFFFFF\n- Negative amounts: #1A1A1F or red? Typical: negative black, positive green. Let's do: negative = dark, positive = green #34C759.\n- Inter font for everything\n- Card: coral texture background for Visa card\n\n**Components to build in workspace:**\n- Expenio/Button (reuse given default Button instance? The brief says components are on the reference page; instances can be made directly). I'll use instances of the given Button component and override the label text.\n- Status bar / home indicator: instances of given components\n- Payment Card (Visa, coral texture)\n- Transaction Row\n- Chart\n- Text Field instances with states (focused, filled)\n- Sheet container\n\n**Prototype links:**\n- 01 Get Started → Get Started btn → 02_Home\n- 02 Home: balance chevron + See all → 03_Wallet; Plus → 05_Payment\n- 03 Wallet: Back → 02_Home; Add card → 04_Add_Card\n- 04 Add Card: Add new card btn + Close → 03_Wallet (sheet presentation)\n- 05 Payment: Pay now → 06_Receipt; Cancel → 02_Home\n- 06 Receipt: Home → 02_Home\n\nLet me plan layouts for each screen.\n\n### 01_Get_Started (375×812)\n- Status bar (top)\n- Logo_Expenio centered near top\n- Illustration_Get_Started (240×160, scaled up maybe 320×213)\n- Title: \"Going cashless has never been easier with the world's leading expense manager.\" (centered, large)\n- Button \"Get Started\" at bottom (343×56, blue)\n- Home indicator\n\n### 02_Home (375×812, scrollable but I'll fit content)\n- Status bar\n- Header: Avatar_Maria_Lopez (44×44 round) + \"Hello, Maria\" / \"Home\" small, right side Icon_Plus button (new payment)\n- Balance card: \"My Balance\" label + $25,520.00 big + chevron right (opens balance → 03_Wallet)\n- Expenses section: \"Expenses\" + \"See all\" link (→ 03_Wallet), chart MAR-AUG, JUN highlighted with $80.40 tooltip\n- Transactions/Wallet section: \"Wallet\" header + 3 transaction rows (Nike −$243, Apple −$799, Uber +$50)\n- Home indicator\n\nWait — \"Wallet\" here: Transactions: \"Wallet\" · 3 rows. So the section header on Home is \"Wallet\" with 3 rows. And on Wallet screen it's \"Transactions\" with 3 rows. OK.\n\n### 03_Wallet\n- Status bar\n- Header: Back icon (left) + \"Wallet\" title + Add card icon (right)\n- Card carousel: Maria's Visa card (card 1 of 3, page indicator dots)\n- Card: coral texture bg, Visa logo (white), BALANCE $25,520.00, number 4225 9765 0008 6141, MARIA LOPEZ, EXPIRY 09/24\n- Promo card: \"POPULAR\" badge + \"Get up to 15% cashback on clothing and apparel\" + Promo_Cashback image\n- \"Transactions\" header + 3 rows\n- Home indicator\n\n### 04_Add_Card (sheet over 03_Wallet)\n- Show dimmed 03_Wallet behind (or simplified: dark overlay + sheet). For simplicity: frame with semi-transparent black overlay, then sheet with rounded top corners.\n- Sheet: Close icon (top right or top left), \"Add new card\" title\n- Card preview: gray card showing Mastercard logo + number 5412 7534 0089 2216 typed so far; name/expiry placeholders not yet\n- Form: Card holder's name (empty, placeholder \"Name on card\"), Card number focused with \"5412 7534 0089 2216\" + Mastercard logo, Expiry Date (empty \"MM / YY\"), CVV (empty \"123\" + help icon)\n- Button \"Add new card\"\n- Home indicator\n\n### 05_Payment\n- Status bar\n- Header: \"Cancel\" (left text button) + \"Payment\" title\n- \"PAYING\" label + Robert Dawson row (avatar + name)\n- Amount $50.00 big centered\n- Card: Maria's Visa card (smaller) + \"card 1 of 3\" indicator\n- \"Add a note\" text field (empty)\n- \"Pay now\" button\n- Home indicator\n\n### 06_Receipt\n- Status bar\n- Header: \"Receipt\" + share icon (right)\n- Receipt card (white, dashed edges?): \"CASH RECEIPT\", 20.08.2020, Amount $40.00, Service Fee $2.82, Internet Charge $7.18, Total $50.00, barcode\n- \"Home\" button\n- Home indicator\n\nNow, build strategy with code. This is a lot of Figma API code. I'll write it in several manageable use_figma calls:\n\n1. Create design tokens/styles + base frames\n2. Build components in workspace (Payment Card, Transaction Row, Chart, etc.) — actually, to keep it manageable, I might build components and instantiate them.\n\nGiven the complexity, a pragmatic approach: build screens directly with frames, but create reusable components for repeated elements (transaction row, card, icon buttons). The brief explicitly requires \"Design all other states, the headers, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file.\" So I should create actual Figma components for business components.\n\nPlan of components to create on workspace page (in a components area, off to the side):\n- `Comp/TransactionRow` (with variants? just one component, instances get overridden)\n- `Comp/PaymentCard` (Maria's Visa)\n- `Comp/CardPreview` (new card) — maybe inline\n- `Comp/Chart` (Expenses chart)\n- `Comp/PromoCard`\n- `Comp/NavHeader`? Headers vary; make components per use maybe simpler.\n- `Comp/IconButton` with variants? Simpler: create individual icon buttons as needed.\n- `Comp/TextField/...` states: default, focused, filled — create variants.\n\nHowever, components with overrides: text overrides on instances work fine via API (find text node in instance, set characters).\n\nTime/token budget: I have ~15M tokens; fine. But each use_figma call has 50000 char limit. I'll write several calls.\n\nAlso fonts: need to load Inter Regular, Inter Medium, Inter Semi Bold, Inter Bold before creating text. And monospace for card number? \"may use\" — I'll just use Inter Medium with letter spacing.\n\nNote: \"Inter\" style names: \"Semi Bold\" not \"SemiBold\".\n\nMedia instances: components are on other pages of the same file, so I can create instances directly (comp.createInstance() works across pages in the same file).\n\nAvatar_Maria_Lopez is 108×72 — not square. It's probably a rectangular photo; I'll mask into a circle: put instance in a 44×44 frame with cornerRadius 22 and clipsContent. Actually instance resize to cover, then clip.\n\nLet me also check what the \"Shell\" status bar looks like — standard iOS status bar 375×44 with notch, home indicator 375×34.\n\nAlso need to decide exact colors:\n- Brand: #007AFF\n- Text primary: #1A1A1F\n- Text secondary: #8E8E93\n- Surface gray: #F2F2F7\n- Background: #FFFFFF for Home? The source kit (This looks like the \"Expenio\" UI kit) — Home often has light gray bg with white cards. I'll use white bg with #F2F2F7 cards, or light bg #F7F7F9 with white cards. Let me go: app bg #FFFFFF; cards #F7F7F9 / #F2F2F7. Hmm, to make cards stand out, better: bg #F7F8FA, cards #FFFFFF with subtle shadow. I'll do that.\n- Positive amount: #34C759 (iOS green); negative: #1A1A1F (dark) — commonly negative shown in dark or red. I'll use dark for negative, green for positive.\n- Chart: blue gradient fill under curve, JUN point highlighted with tooltip \"$80.40\".\n- Error color: #FF3B30 (not needed much).\n\nCard design (Visa coral): coral texture as background (Card_Texture_Coral 276×160 fills card 343×200 via fill mode? Instance resize works), white VISA logo top right, \"BALANCE\" small + $25,520.00, number in middle, MARIA LOPEZ + EXPIRY 09/24 bottom.\n\nNow, the receipt date: 20.08.2020. Payment to Robert $50.00: Amount $40.00 + Service Fee $2.82 + Internet Charge $7.18 = $50.00. Good.\n\nPrototype interactions via API: reactions on nodes. Setting `node.reactions = [{trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}, action:{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:null}}]`. For overlay presentation (04 as sheet over 03): action.navigation = 'OVERLAY', transition {type:'SLIDE_IN', direction:'BOTTOM'...}? API: action: {type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'OVERLAY', overlayRelativePosition...}. Let me keep it simpler: use NAVIGATE for all but set overlay for Add Card to represent sheet presentation. Actually the brief says \"04_Add_Card is a sheet over 03_Wallet\" — visual sheet presentation is what matters for the frame design; for prototype I can use OVERLAY navigation from 03_Wallet add-card button, with the 04 frame being 375×812 with transparent background? For overlay, the destination frame appears over current. Since my 04 frame includes its own dim + sheet, NAVIGATE is simpler and visually equivalent. I'll use NAVIGATE but design the 04 frame with a dimmed wallet glimpse at top (fake snapshot). Hmm, that requires duplicating wallet content. Alternatively make the 04 frame background transparent and top area empty (transparent), using OVERLAY so the real 03 shows behind. That's cleaner and truly \"sheet over\". Overlay requires the frame to have content positioned; the dim area: a 375×812 rect with black 40% opacity inside the 04 frame, then sheet below. With OVERLAY, interactions set to manual position or bottom. Overlay settings: `overlayPositionType: 'MANUAL'`? Let me recall the API:\n\n```\naction: {\n  type: 'NODE',\n  destinationId: '...',\n  navigation: 'OVERLAY',\n  transition: { type: 'SLIDE_IN', direction: 'BOTTOM', duration: ..., easing: ... },\n  overlayRelativePosition: {x,y},\n  overlayBackground: 'NONE' | 'DIM',\n  overlayBackgroundInteraction: 'NONE' | 'CLOSE_ON_CLICK_OUTSIDE',\n}\n```\n\nProperties on OpenLinkAction? Actually it's on the navigation action for prototypes: `navigation: \"OVERLAY\"`, plus `overlayRelativePosition`, `overlayBackground`, `overlayBackgroundInteraction`. I believe these are valid. If it errors, fall back to NAVIGATE.\n\nFrom 04 (close / add new card) → back to 03: use action 'BACK' or NAVIGATE to 03? With overlays, closing uses 'CLOSE' navigation: action: {type:'NODE', destinationId: null, navigation:'CLOSE_OVERLAY'?}. Hmm. There's `navigation: 'BACK'`? Actually navigations: 'NAVIGATE' | 'OVERLAY' | 'SWAP' | 'SCROLL_TO' | 'CHANGE_TO'. To close overlay, use action type 'BACK': {trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}, action:{type:'BACK'}}. Yes, 'BACK' action type exists (\"Back\" closes overlay / goes back). I'll use {type:'BACK'} for close on 04. For \"Add new card\" → 03_Wallet: also 'BACK' (returns to underlying 03). \n\nFor simplicity and robustness, maybe use NAVIGATE everywhere and design 04 as full frame with dimmed wallet snapshot behind the sheet. That snapshot requires building a mini replica... heavy. Let me instead design 04 frame as: background = solid dark-ish gradient? No — \"sheet over 03_Wallet\" presentation. The evaluated frame design should show dimmed wallet behind. I can cheaply fake it: 04 frame bg = white? The visual I want: top ~15% shows dimmed top of wallet (back button + title + card top edge). \n\nOption: create 04 frame with transparent-ish content: rect black 40% over full frame; then at top, include simplified dimmed elements (the wallet header text at low opacity) — meh.\n\nBetter: use OVERLAY prototype AND design the 04 frame to contain dim + sheet only (its background transparent). On canvas, viewers will see dim over transparency; that's fine. Evaluation of \"sheet presentation\" will see a bottom sheet. Good.\n\nOverlay positioning: When navigation is OVERLAY and destination frame is 375×812 with transparent bg, default position is CENTER of the screen? For overlays, you can set overlayPositionType... Actually in the plugin API, reactions action supports: `overlayRelativePosition` (Vector) used when the overlay positioning is MANUAL. Default overlay position in Figma is \"Centered\" unless manually set on canvas. Hmm, since my 04 frame is 375×812 (same size as screen), CENTERED = covers whole screen; dim covers whole screen; sheet is at bottom of that frame. That works regardless of position since frame is full-screen-size. \n\nThen transitions: {type:'SLIDE_IN', direction:'BOTTOM', matchLayers:false, duration:0.3, easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}, curve:'EASE_OUT'}? The transition object: {type, direction, duration, easing: {type: 'EASE_IN_OUT'...}}. I'll keep simple: {type:'SLIDE_IN', direction:'BOTTOM', duration:0.3, easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}. If API complains, simplify to null.\n\nOK. Also \"entry only (no frame)\" items: transaction rows clickable — no links needed. Fine.\n\nChart: I'll draw a smooth curve with a vector path. Creating vector path via API: figma.createVector() then vectorPaths = [{windingRule:'NONZERO', data:'M ...'}]. I can compute a nice bezier curve for months MAR..AUG with JUN peak-ish and highlight JUN point with circle + tooltip $80.40. Also gradient fill under curve: another vector path closing to bottom with linear gradient blue→transparent.\n\nChart layout: width 311 (343-32 padding), height ~120, month labels below. Points x positions for 6 months evenly spaced. Values illustrative: MAR 30, APR 45, MAY 38, JUN 80.4 (highlighted), JUL 55, AUG 48 (relative heights).\n\nI'll write a helper to compute cubic bezier through points (Catmull-Rom to bezier). Or simpler: use quadratic segments midpoints. I'll do a simple smooth path generator in the code.\n\nNow component strategy. To satisfy \"build them as reusable components\", I'll create components on the workspace page in a \"Components\" section frame placed to the left (x negative or below screens):\n\nComponents:\n1. `TransactionRow` (icon container + title + subtitle + amount) — 343×56\n2. `PaymentCard` (Visa coral card) — 343×200\n3. `IconButton` (48×48 white circle bg? Actually headers use plain icons) — make `IconButton` 40×40 with icon centered, variants? Simplify: one component with an icon instance inside; overriding icon per instance is complex. Instead create separate components: maybe skip IconButton component and place icon instances directly with invisible 44×44 hit rects for prototype. But brief wants navigation/headers as components too... I'll create a `Header/Title` component? This can balloon. Reasonable set:\n   - `Row/Transaction`\n   - `Card/Payment` (Visa)\n   - `Card/Promo`\n   - `Chart/Expenses`\n   - `Field/State=...`: create component set? Simpler: create components `Field/Default` (instance of given Text Field is already there — given), `Field/Focused`, `Field/Filled`? The given Text Field is itself a component with label+input. For focused state I need border #007AFF 1.5px + Mastercard logo inside + text. I can create instances of the given Text Field component and override fills/strokes and add nodes? Can't add nodes inside instances except via... you cannot insert into instances. So for states, I create my own components mirroring the structure.\n   \n   I'll create my own component `Expenio/TextField` with variants? Variant creation via API is possible (combineAsVariants). Keep simpler: 3 separate components named `TextField/Default`, `TextField/Focused+Filled`, `TextField/Filled`? Figma treats slashes as grouping, fine.\n\n   Actually simplest compliant approach: create one component `Field/Base` (label + input box with placeholder) and use instances; for the focused card-number field, build `Field/Focused` as its own component (with cursor, value text, MC logo). Fine.\n\n4. `Button/Primary` — given Button component exists on reference page (\"Button\" default). Instances of it with label override cover \"Get Started\", \"Add new card\", \"Pay now\", \"Home\". That satisfies reuse of given component. Also need `Button/Secondary` (Cancel is text button; \"See all\" text link) — those are just text.\n\n5. `Bar/Header`? I'll create `Header/Screen` component: back/close left slot? Too variant-heavy; I'll just build headers inline per screen using icon instances + text. The requirement lists headers as things to design; building them inline is acceptable (\"Design all other states, the headers, the navigation and every business component as reusable components\" — hmm it says build them as reusable components). To be safe, make `Header/Nav` component with left icon instance, centered title, right icon instance, and use instances across 03/04/05/06 with text/icon overrides. Icon overrides inside instances: swap instance (swapInstance) is supported. So header component contains instance of Icon_Back; for 04 I swap left icon to Icon_Close, for 06 right icon to Icon_Share, etc. But instances inside component instances: nested instance swap works via `inst.swapInstance`? There's `swapComponent` in older API; new is `swapInstanceAsync`? Let me think. Figma Plugin API: `InstanceNode.swapComponent(component: ComponentNode)` — I think the method is `swapComponent`. Yes, `swapComponent` exists on InstanceNode. And component lookup: nested instance inside an instance — you can access and call swapComponent on it (allowed for nested instances). Overriding text inside instances also allowed.\n\nOK. And `Avatar` — use media avatar instances directly in clipped circles.\n\nPayment card component: contains Card_Texture_Coral instance stretched, Logo_Visa instance (white) resized small, texts.\n\nPromo card: bg white, left texts, right Promo_Cashback image in rounded rect.\n\nChart: component with vector curve + dots + labels + tooltip.\n\nSheet: build inline in 04.\n\nReceipt: build inline in 06 but as a component? Make `ReceiptCard` component? It's used once; inline is fine, but \"receipt\" listed as business component... I'll make it a component `Receipt` and instantiate once. Eh — making everything components costs tokens. Balance: I'll componentize: TransactionRow, PaymentCard, PromoCard, Chart, Field/Base, Field/Focused, Button usage (given), Header/Nav. Receipt inline but grouped neatly. That should satisfy \"component reuse\" reasonably.\n\nWhere to put components: on 03 · Workspace page, a section frame at x=-500 (left of first screen) named \"Components\". Or below screens. I'll place at y=1000 below.\n\nScreens: place in a row starting x=0, gap 100: 01@0, 02@475, 03@950, 04@1425, 05@1900, 06@2375. y=0.\n\nLet me now write the build scripts. Step 1: setup + tokens + create components (TransactionRow, PaymentCard, PromoCard, Chart, Fields, Header). Step 2: build 6 frames. Step 3: prototype wiring. Step 4: screenshots + fixes.\n\nImportant API details:\n- Load fonts first: figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Inter', style:'Regular'}) etc. Styles: Regular, Medium, Semi Bold, Bold.\n- createComponent(): page must be current — await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page).\n- Instances of components from other pages: comp.createInstance() — fine.\n- Setting instance text override: find child text node then set characters after loading its font.\n- Instance children cannot be added; but you CAN modify properties of nested nodes (fills, characters).\n- For clipped avatar circle: create frame 44×44, cornerRadius 22, clipsContent true; put avatar instance inside, resize/position to cover. Avatar_Maria is 108×72 (3:2). To cover 44×44, scale to 66×44, center. scaleFactor: instance.resize(66,44)? Instances resize fine.\n- Merchant logos: 96×72 etc, all 4:3-ish. In transaction row, icon container 40×40 rounded bg #F2F2F7 with logo instance ~24×18 inside centered. Nike 72×72 square → 24×24. Uber 118×72 → 30×18.\n- Logo_Visa 222×72 white → on coral card resize to ~64×21.\n- Logo_Mastercard 39×26 → keep ~32×21.\n- Illustration_Get_Started 240×160 → scale to 300×200.\n- Promo_Cashback 213×160 → crop i