{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":30985,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"02216ae685fb0a7a471cfbec65a9de9b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Components created. Now build the 6 screens. Let me do them in batches: Screen 01 Get Started, Screen 02 Home, then 03/04, then 05/06, then wire prototype.\n\nScreen 01_Get_Started at (0,0), 375×812:\n- white bg\n- status bar (1:33)\n- Logo centered y~120\n- Illustration 240×160 at x=67, y~180 — maybe scale bigger: illustration is 240×160; place at 67, 190 at size 240×160 or slightly larger 280? Instance resize 240×160 fine; could place at (67,190). Actually center x = (375-240)/2 = 67.5.\n- Headline copy 20px SemiBold centered, x=40 w=295, y=420\n- Button instance at (16, y=690), text \"Get Started\"\n- Home indicator at bottom y=778 (812-34)\n\nScreen 02_Home at (450, 0), 375×812, light gray bg #FAFAFC:\n- status bar\n- Greeting row y=60: Avatar (40) at x=16 + \"Hello, Maria\" 20 semibold + right: plus FAB 44x44 circle blue with Icon_Plus white\n- Balance card white r=20 shadow at (16, 116) w=343 h=108: \"My Balance\" 13 medium gray at top-left, \"$25,520.00\" 28 bold, right chevron icon (light circle bg 36x36 with chevron 16)\n- Expenses card white r=20 at (16, 244) w=343 h=232: header \"Expenses\" 17 semibold, right maybe period? Keep just \"Expenses\". Chart instance at y+56 (x=16 padding). Chart width 311 = 343-32.\n- Transactions: \"Wallet\" header 17 semibold + \"See all\" 13 medium blue right, y=500; rows at y=528: 3 transaction rows (64 each = 192). Rows: Nike −$243.00 15 Aug 2020, Apple iPad Pro 2020 −$799.00 10 Aug 2020, Uber +$50.00 (green) 5 Mar 2020. Rows have merchant logos swapped: Nike → 5:9, Apple → 5:5, Uber → 5:7. The TransactionRow component instance default logo is Nike (5:9); for Apple and Uber rows, need to swap the inner instance's component. Instances of components inside instances can be swapped via swapComponent on the inner instance? Inner instances within an instance can be modified. Actually you cannot swapComponent on an instance nested inside another instance? You can — instances inside instances are accessible and modifiable (except structure changes like swap? I believe swapComponent works on nested instances too since it's not a structural change). Let me try; if it fails, fallback: detach? Instead, I'll make the merchant logo swapping by simply hiding and adding? Hmm. Alternative: don't nest logo in component; keep component with placeholder and add merchant logo instance on top in the screen. But then component reuse suffers slightly. Try swapComponent first.\n\n- Home indicator.\n\nScreen 03_Wallet at (900, 0):\n- status bar, header nav (Back left, \"Wallet\", Add_Card right)\n- Card at (16, 108): payment card instance w=343. Below: pagination dots 3 (active wide) + label \"Card 1 of 3\"? Must include \"card 1 of 3 in the wallet\". I'll add dots and small text \"Card 1 of 3\" maybe centered under card. Dots centered y=320; text under? Use dots: 3 dots, active is 18 wide pill blue, others 6 gray. Add text \"1 of 3\"? The must-include says \"card 1 of 3 in the wallet\" — represent via pagination showing card 1 of 3. I'll add dots + small caption \"Card 1 of 3\". Fine.\n- Promo card at y=352\n- \"Transactions\" header + See all? not required on wallet; just \"Transactions\". Rows y=496: 3 rows.\n- Home indicator.\n\nScreen 04_Add_Card at (1350, 0):\n- Full 375×812: dim overlay (black 0.4) over a background suggestion of Wallet. Since the sheet is over 03_Wallet, simplest: bg = white full frame, then dim layer full size, then sheet. But must show sheet presentation. I'll put a mini card hint? Actually to convey \"sheet over wallet\": I can clone the wallet screen content behind? That's heavy. Common approach in the original kit: sheet occupies lower portion with handle, and behind shows dimmed wallet card area. I'll do: background white; at top show status bar; dim rectangle 375×812 black 45%; then sheet from y=210 to 812: white r=24 top corners, handle bar at y=224, header \"Add new card\" centered 17 semibold at y=240, close icon right at 335,y=240 (in circle?).\n- Card preview: new Mastercard card at (32, 284) w=311 h=184 — build inline (not component): dark charcoal bg (#26262E) rounded 20, Mastercard logo top-right, number \"5412 7534 0089 2216\" white 16 spaced, placeholders \"CARD HOLDER NAME\" and \"MM/YY\" in white 40%. Label \"NEW CARD\"? no. Name/expiry not yet entered — show placeholder text.\n- Form: Field Focused component instance (Card number) at (16, 496); Row y=585: compact field instance (Expiry Date) at x=16 w=164 (need to hide help icon for expiry), compact instance for CVV at x=196: change label \"CVV\", placeholder \"123\", help icon visible.\n- Button \"Add new card\" at (16, 690) — reuse Button component, set text.\n- Home indicator.\n\nWait — compact field component has help icon; for expiry hide it. Instance overrides allow visibility toggle. Good.\n\nAlso the button label default \"Get Started\"; change characters to \"Add new card\" — instance text override works.\n\nScreen 05_Payment at (1800, 0):\n- status bar; header: \"Cancel\" text 16 medium blue at left (x16 y~70), \"Payment\" centered 17 semibold.\n- PAYING label 11 medium gray letterspaced, y=128, x=16? Center design: payee centered? I'll do left-aligned section style consistent with home. Actually a nicer layout: centered payee: avatar 72 centered, \"PAYING\" above small, \"Robert Dawson\" name below 17 semibold, then big amount \"$50.00\" 40 bold centered, then note field, then card section, then Pay now button.\nLayout: \n- y=64: Cancel left; \"Payment\" center.\n- y=116: \"PAYING\" centered 11 medium gray ls 1.5\n- y=140: Avatar Robert 72×72 centered (x=151.5)\n- y=222: \"Robert Dawson\" 17 semibold centered\n- y=258: \"$50.00\" 44 bold centered\n- y=330: note field: rounded surface box w=343 h=48 with placeholder \"Add a note\" left, maybe pencil? Just text.\n- y=402: label \"FROM\"? not required. Card: payment card instance at (16, 402) w=343 h=200. Plus dots \"card 1 of 3\" under (y=614).\n- Button \"Pay now\" at (16, 690).\n- Home indicator.\n\nScreen 06_Receipt at (2250, 0):\n- status bar; header \"Receipt\" centered y=64; share icon right (circle).\n- Receipt card white r=20 shadow at (16, 116) w=343 h=~480: \n  - \"CASH RECEIPT\" 12 semibold letterspaced centered y+28\n  - \"20.08.2020\" 12 regular gray centered\n  - dashed divider\n  - rows: Amount $40.00, Service Fee $2.82, Internet Charge $7.18 — label 14 regular gray left, value 14 medium ink right\n  - dashed divider\n  - Total $50.00 — 16 semibold\n  - barcode centered at bottom y+~380, 254×68 → scale to 220×59? Keep 254×68 fits within 343-64 padding. x=(343-254)/2=44.5.\n- Button \"Home\" at (16, 690).\n- Home indicator.\n\nPrototype flows after screens: \n- 01: button → 02 (on tap navigate)\n- 02: chevron (balance) → 03; \"See all\" → 03; plus button → 05\n- 03: back icon → 02; add card icon → 04 (overlay? \"sheet over\" — could use Open Overlay, but simpler navigate; brief says sheet presentation; I'll use navigate to 04 since 04 itself renders the sheet; or use overlay. Use \"NAVIGATE\" for reliability.)\n- 04: close → 03; Add new card button → 03\n- 05: Cancel → 02; Pay now → 06\n- 06: Home button → 02; share → entry only, no link.\n\nNote: reactions on instances/nested: set reactions on specific nodes. For nested nodes inside instances (e.g., chevron icon inside my own built balance card — the balance card is built inline in screen, not component, so nodes are directly accessible). The header nav component instances: left/right icons are inside instance; prototype reactions can be set on nested instance children? Reactions can be added to instances (any node supports reactions). Setting reaction on a nested node inside an instance — allowed? I believe reactions can be set on instance children. Yes, in Figma you can add prototype interactions to elements inside instances. Via API, node.reactions = [...] should work on nested instance children too.\n\nLet me build screens 01 and 02 now.\n\nFor swapping merchant logo in transaction rows: try rowInstance.findOne(n => n.name === 'Merchant_Nike'...) — inner instance name will be \"Merchant_Nike\" (component name). swapComponent(uberComp). I'll attempt; wrap in try.\n\nAlso note Avatar_Maria_Lopez component is 108×72 (includes maybe background?). From screenshot, avatar shows a photo ~72×72 with rounded corners? It looked like a square photo. The component 108 wide might include some decoration. I'll resize to 40×40 proportionally? 108×72 aspect 1.5 — hmm that's odd for an avatar. Looking at media screenshot: Avatar_Maria_Lopez appears as a rounded square photo ~ that area. The label below said component is 108×72. Maybe it has 3 avatars stacked? Screenshot shows one photo though, ~55px wide in a 1296-scaled image where cell is 114px... Actually the image at scale 0.926: cell width 114*0.926≈105, photo appears ~60px wide → ~65 real px. Hmm, component w=108 h=72. Wait maybe the component contains the photo (72×72) plus nothing? Let me just inspect the avatar component children quickly in the next call before using. Similarly check Logo_Visa aspect (222×72 seems wide; might include white padding? Visa logo white text on transparent). And Illustration, Card texture are fine.\n\nLet me inspect these media components' structure quickly, then build screens.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"40af89c4-d68b-44d7-a56d-c7fe152ae445","uuid":"84af64db-6278-439c-a8d9-0d63a99d86e2","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:22:20.716Z","thinking_duration_ms":60839}
